<td id="A3.T9.12.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A3.T9.12.16.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">1000</span></td>
<td id="A3.T9.12.16.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A3.T9.12.16.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">39.2</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A3.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ Speedup Comparison ‣ Appendix C About Progressive Step Reduction ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Don’t Let It Fade: Preserving Edits in Diffusion Language Models via Token Timestep Allocation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> summarizes relative decoding speed ratios (GPT-2 <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">base<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=1.0</annotation></semantics></math></span>); for diffusion-based methods, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of inference steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Hyperparameter Sensitivity</h3>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Effect of Control Hyperparameter <math id="A4.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<figure id="A4.T10" class="ltx_table">
