<td id="A4.T10.6.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.86</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.6.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T10.6.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">2</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">42.6</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">15.8</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.3.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.86</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.6.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T10.6.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">20</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">56.2</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">16.3</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.85</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.6.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T10.6.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">200</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">74.1</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">19.4</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.83</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.6.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T10.6.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">2000</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">90.1</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">26.8</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.6.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.85</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T10.6.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T10.6.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">20000</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">94.2</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.7.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">42.4</span></td>
<td id="A4.T10.6.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding:-2.3pt 4.0pt;"><span id="A4.T10.6.7.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.90</span></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The generation quality of controllable diffusion is highly sensitive to the choice of the control hyperparameter <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout our experiments, we select the optimal <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> from the range <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{2,20,200,2000,20000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>20000</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{2,20,200,2000,20000\}</annotation></semantics></math> based on its effectiveness in achieving a balance between accuracy and fluency.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A4.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ D.1 Effect of Control Hyperparameter 𝜆 ‣ Appendix D Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Don’t Let It Fade: Preserving Edits in Diffusion Language Models via Token Timestep Allocation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> presents the impact of different <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> values on the sentiment control task. A higher <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> generally leads to increased accuracy but at the cost of reduced fluency, reflecting the well-known trade-off between control strength and naturalness. Among the tested values, <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=2000</annotation></semantics></math> provides the best balance between accuracy and fluency, making it our choice for sentiment control.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The effect of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> follows a similar trend across other tasks as well. Consequently, we determine the optimal <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for each task by selecting the value that best balances these two competing objectives.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.26200v1/figures/smoothing_graph.png" id="A4.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:286/191;" width="286" height="191" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A4.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A4.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Effect of smoothing factor on (a) Sentiment accuracy and (b) Perplexity.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Smoothing Factor</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To regulate the balance between the global timestep and the adaptive token timestep, we introduce a smoothing factor, defined as follows:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{i}^{\mathrm{final}}\;=\;\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}\,t\;+\;(1-\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}})\,t_{i}^{\mathrm{adaptive}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>final</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>adaptive</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{i}^{\mathrm{final}}\;=\;\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}\,t\;+\;(1-\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}})\,t_{i}^{\mathrm{adaptive}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In our experiments, we set <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math>, as it provides an optimal trade-off between accuracy and fluency. To examine the impact of this factor, we conduct a sentiment control task, generating 600 samples for each value of <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the range of 0.0 to 1.0. Here, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a purely adaptive gradient schedule, while <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math> represents a constant schedule.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ D.1 Effect of Control Hyperparameter 𝜆 ‣ Appendix D Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Don’t Let It Fade: Preserving Edits in Diffusion Language Models via Token Timestep Allocation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> illustrates the effect of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}</annotation></semantics></math> on both accuracy and fluency. As shown in Figure <a href="#A4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ D.1 Effect of Control Hyperparameter 𝜆 ‣ Appendix D Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Don’t Let It Fade: Preserving Edits in Diffusion Language Models via Token Timestep Allocation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>(a), accuracy tends to decrease as <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\mathrm{smooth}}</annotation></semantics></math> increases from 0 to 1, supporting our hypothesis that adaptive scheduling enhances key token preservation. For fluency, rather than exhibiting a monotonous decrease in perplexity, a U-shaped trend emerges, with the lowest perplexity observed within the range of 0.4 to 0.8, as depicted in Figure <a href="#A4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ D.1 Effect of Control Hyperparameter 𝜆 ‣ Appendix D Hyperparameter Sensitivity ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Don’t Let It Fade: Preserving Edits in Diffusion Language Models via Token Timestep Allocation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>(b).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Detailed Results</h3>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Sentiment Control</h4>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present sentiment-controlled generation results using the fully progressively reduced models in Table <a href="#A5.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ E.1 Sentiment Control ‣ Appendix E Detailed Results ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Don’t Let It Fade: Preserving Edits in Diffusion Language Models via Token Timestep Allocation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. All results are reported under a fixed control strength of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=2000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=2000</annotation></semantics></math>, with adaptive timestep allocation (smoothing factor = 0.6) and two control iterations. Under the same configuration, Table <a href="#A5.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ E.1 Sentiment Control ‣ Appendix E Detailed Results ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Don’t Let It Fade: Preserving Edits in Diffusion Language Models via Token Timestep Allocation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> compares adaptive and constant allocation strategies for TTA(200) and TTA(50), focusing on inference steps fewer than 100.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T11" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span>Accuracy (Acc) and Perplexity (PPL) across different inference steps and training-time TTA schedules for sentiment control task. (Iter 2)</figcaption>
<table id="A5.T11.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.T11.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.T11.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.9pt;padding-bottom:-0.9pt;"><span id="A5.T11.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">T</span></td>
<td id="A5.T11.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.9pt;padding-bottom:-0.9pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A5.T11.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">TTA (5000)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T11.5.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.9pt;padding-bottom:-0.9pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A5.T11.5.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">TTA (1000)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T11.5.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.9pt;padding-bottom:-0.9pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A5.T11.5.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">TTA (200)</span></td>
<td id="A5.T11.5.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:-0.9pt;padding-bottom:-0.9pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A5.T11.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">TTA (50)</span></td>
